Summary of modifications in this project:
  - gc_correction/griffin_GC_counts.py: optimized GC counting (C-level fast
    path with an exact, seeded fallback for ambiguous bases), itertuples
    iteration, finer parallel chunking, and pandas>=2.0 compatible
    aggregation. Output is bit-identical to the original.
  - gc_correction/griffin_GC_bias.py: replaced removed pandas .append calls
    with pd.concat (output unchanged); added an optional --no_plots flag and a
    headless-safe matplotlib backend; smoothing left unchanged.
  - common/manifest.py: helper to read/write samples.GC.yaml (the format is
    byte-compatible with the original Griffin snakefile output).
  - workflows/run_gc_correction.sh: terminal driver (no Snakemake/SLURM).
  - tests/: correctness, regression, and demo-comparison scripts.
